.github/workflows/*.lock.yml linguist-generated=true

# Index and log files grow by appending: a new item, a new person, a new entry. When two agents append at once,
# git calls it a conflict and one run's entire work is discarded — around 90 AI credits and a turn of story, to
# avoid interleaving two lines that were never really in competition. `union` keeps both sides instead. Order can
# come out odd and a duplicate is possible; the Custodian tidies those, and a tidy-up is far cheaper than a lost
# run. Deliberately NOT applied to files an agent rewrites wholesale (state.md, a site page, a quest), where
# keeping both sides would produce duplicated prose rather than a merged list.
codex/chronicle/**/*.md merge=union
codex/**/README.md merge=union